  "question": {
    "text": "If the area bounded by the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and outside the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> is A, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to __________."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "42",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>slope</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>is</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now plotting the diagram of the above function we have,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0042_e25ed0512562.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 273px;\" /></p><p>So, required area is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mn>360</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msubsup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msubsup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>42</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
